{
  "reading": "Asked: what to cut for Tataru Taru on jaws-v1. Tataru is a 0/3 Dwarf, not a Human, so Shabraz cannot fly it; Scions' Secretary fires once per turn, so a wheel turn yields one tapped Treasure, not three. Its realistic output is its ETB (a draw plus a Treasure if the opponent takes the card), one Treasure per wheel turn or Willie Lumpkin hit, and one per Faerie Mastermind activation on an opponent's turn. It is the fifth card in the thinnest pillar (artifact-token makers: Big Score, Jaws, Prismari Command, Smothering Tithe; 82.5% measured), and ramp sits at 12 (top of 10-12), so a rock is the cut that costs least.",
  "log_entries_read": ["003", "007"],
  "axes_engaged": [
    {"axis": "ramp", "verdict": "adequate", "measured": {"value": "12"}, "reading": "At the top of the 10-12 band, so one rock out leaves 11, still in band; Tataru's tapped Treasure is not turn-2 ramp."},
    {"axis": "interaction", "verdict": "adequate", "measured": {"value": "8"}, "reading": "Exactly at target; Collective Defiance is one of the eight, so cutting it puts the deck under."}
  ],
  "cut_candidates": [
    {"card": "Talisman of Conviction", "why": "The rock that overlaps most: W is 2 sources over target, and a sitting rock is never Jaws fodder, while a Treasure is.", "cost_of_cutting": "One turn-2 mana source; R falls 1 under target (try's colour check), and the turn-4 Shabraz slightly weaker on the 2-drop.", "difficulty": "contested", "orphans_stack": []},
    {"card": "Collective Defiance", "why": "Study 006 filed it with the old ping plan; RR sorcery whose wheel hits one player.", "cost_of_cutting": "Interaction drops from 8 to 7, under target; the wheel count drops from 10 to 9 (try: finisher wheel by T8 79.8% -> 76.3%, [-3.9, -3.1]); a 4-damage creature answer is gone.", "difficulty": "painful", "orphans_stack": []},
    {"card": "Fellwar Stone", "why": "The weakest rock (depends on opponents' lands), named in CONTEXT's mana plan.", "cost_of_cutting": "U and R each fall 1 under target (try); one turn-2 rock gone.", "difficulty": "contested", "orphans_stack": []}
  ],
  "add_candidates": [
    {"card": "Tataru Taru", "closes": "An artifact token maker drawn", "source": "prompt", "why": "Fifth member of the thinnest pillar; ETB draw grows Shabraz; turns wheel turns into Jaws fodder.", "natural_cut": "Talisman of Conviction"}
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    {"question": "Do opponents at this table take Tataru's optional ETB card (which is what makes the Treasure)?", "settled_by": "goldfish", "why_it_matters": "If they decline, the ETB is a plain cantrip and the engine needs a wheel or Mastermind to fire at all."}
  ],
  "gaps": ["No Forge record for Tataru; the goldfish has no opponents, so it cannot price the extra card each ETB or Willie hit hands an opponent.", "Sokka was screened and rejected as a cut: a Human that draws on attack is on-plan, which the goldfish cannot see."]
}
